{"type":"message","id":"651093e2","parentId":"14f4ccd1","timestamp":"2026-02-12T11:25:52.444Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Checking test commands in docs**","thinkingSignature":"{\"encrypted_content\":\"\",\"id\":\"\",\"summary\":[{\"text\":\"**Checking test commands in docs**\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"}],\"type\":\"reasoning\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_AG1GDzV9MNsIyqxVDvu389Vy|","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"C:\\Users\\Raitis\\Desktop\\My WEB projects\\SEOIndicator-com\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\docs\\AUTO-TESTS-SETUP.md"},"partialJson":"{\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Raitis\\\\Desktop\\\\My WEB projects\\\\SEOIndicator-com\\\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\\\docs\\\\AUTO-TESTS-SETUP.md\"}"}],"api":"openai-responses","provider":"github-copilot","model":"gpt-5.2-codex","usage":{"input":293,"output":78,"cacheRead":7808,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":8179,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770895550378}}
{"type":"message","id":"02082e95","parentId":"651093e2","timestamp":"2026-02-12T11:25:52.470Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_AG1GDzV9MNsIyqxVDvu389Vy|","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# GitHub Actions CI/CD Setup for Playwright Tests\r\n\r\nThis document explains how to set up and use GitHub Actions for running Playwright tests automatically.\r\n\r\n## Workflow Overview\r\n\r\nThe GitHub Actions workflow (`.github/workflows/playwright.yml`) is configured to:\r\n\r\n- **Trigger**: Run on pushes and pull requests to `main` and `develop` branches\r\n- **Environment**: Ubuntu latest with Node.js LTS\r\n- **Browsers**: Chromium with system dependencies\r\n- **Artifacts**: Upload test reports and results for 30 days\r\n\r\n## Workflow Steps\r\n\r\n1. **Checkout code** - Downloads your repository\r\n2. **Setup Node.js** - Installs Node.js LTS with npm caching\r\n3. **Install dependencies** - Runs `npm ci` for faster, reliable installs\r\n4. **Install Playwright browsers** - Installs Chromium with system dependencies\r\n5. **Run tests** - Executes all Playwright tests\r\n6. **Upload artifacts** - Saves test reports and results for debugging\r\n\r\n## Key Features\r\n\r\n### ✅ Modern Approach\r\n- Uses the **recommended Playwright CLI** approach instead of the deprecated GitHub Action\r\n- Based on [Microsoft's official documentation](https://github.com/microsoft/playwright-github-action)\r\n\r\n### ✅ Performance Optimized\r\n- **npm ci** for faster dependency installation\r\n- **Node.js caching** to speed up builds\r\n- **Single browser** (Chromium) for faster execution\r\n- **Parallel test execution** where possible\r\n\r\n### ✅ Robust Error Handling\r\n- **60-minute timeout** prevents hanging builds\r\n- **Artifact upload** on both success and failure\r\n- **Retry logic** for flaky tests (2 retries on CI)\r\n\r\n### ✅ Developer Friendly\r\n- **HTML reports** for easy debugging\r\n- **Test artifacts** available for download\r\n- **Clear step naming** for easy troubleshooting\r\n\r\n## Setup Instructions\r\n\r\n### 1. Repository Setup\r\n```bash\r\n# Ensure your repository has the following files:\r\n# - .github/workflows/playwright.yml\r\n# - package.json\r\n# - playwright.config.js\r\n# - tests/ directory with your test files\r\n```\r\n\r\n### 2. Push to GitHub\r\n```bash\r\ngit add .\r\ngit commit -m \"Add Playwright tests with GitHub Actions\"\r\ngit push origin main\r\n```\r\n\r\n### 3. Monitor Results\r\n- Go to your repository on GitHub\r\n- Click the \"Actions\" tab\r\n- View the workflow runs and results\r\n- Download artifacts if tests fail\r\n\r\n## Local Testing\r\n\r\nTest your CI setup locally:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n# Install dependencies\r\nnpm ci\r\n\r\n# Install browsers with system dependencies (like CI)\r\nnpm run install:browsers\r\n\r\n# Run tests in CI mode\r\nnpm run test:ci\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Customization\r\n\r\n### Change Trigger Branches\r\nEdit `.github/workflows/playwright.yml`:\r\n```yaml\r\non:\r\n  push:\r\n    branches: [ main, develop, feature/* ]  # Add your branches\r\n  pull_request:\r\n    branches: [ main ]  # Only main branch PRs\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Add More Browsers\r\nEdit `playwright.config.js`:\r\n```javascript\r\nprojects: [\r\n  {\r\n    name: 'chromium',\r\n    use: { ...devices['Desktop Chrome'] },\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    name: 'firefox',  // Uncomment this\r\n    use: { ...devices['Desktop Firefox'] },\r\n  },\r\n]\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Change Artifact Retention\r\nEdit `.github/workflows/playwright.yml`:\r\n```yaml\r\nretention-days: 7  # Keep artifacts for 7 days instead of 30\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Troubleshooting\r\n\r\n### Tests Fail in CI but Pass Locally\r\n- Check if your local server is running (CI doesn't have your local server)\r\n- Consider using `webServer` configuration in `playwright.config.js`\r\n- Verify environment variables and secrets\r\n\r\n### Common CI Issues\r\n- **Missing package-lock.json**: Run `npm install` locally to generate the lock file\r\n- **Artifact upload warnings**: The workflow uses `if-no-files-found: ignore` to handle empty directories gracefully\r\n- **Browser installation**: The workflow uses `--with-deps` flag for system dependencies\r\n\r\n### Browser Installation Fails\r\n- The workflow uses `--with-deps` flag for system dependencies\r\n- Check GitHub Actions logs for specific error messages\r\n- Ensure sufficient disk space in the runner\r\n\r\n### Timeout Issues\r\n- Increase timeout in workflow: `timeout-minutes: 120`\r\n- Optimize tests to run faster\r\n- Consider running fewer browsers in CI\r\n\r\n## Best Practices\r\n\r\n1. **Keep tests fast** - CI should complete in under 10 minutes\r\n2. **Use specific selectors** - Avoid flaky tests\r\n3. **Test critical paths** - Focus on user journeys\r\n4. **Regular maintenance** - Update Playwright and dependencies\r\n5. **Monitor results** - Check CI runs regularly\r\n\r\n## Resources\r\n\r\n- [Playwright GitHub Action Documentation](https://github.com/microsoft/playwright-github-action)\r\n- [Playwright CI/CD Guide](https://playwright.dev/docs/ci)\r\n- [GitHub Actions Documentation](https://docs.github.com/en/actions)\r\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770895552467}}
{"type":"message","id":"25a4b8cd","parentId":"02082e95","timestamp":"2026-02-12T11:25:54.663Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Checking test command in package.json**","thinkingSignature":"{\"encrypted_content\":\"\",\"id\":\"\",\"summary\":[{\"text\":\"**Checking test command in package.json**\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"}],\"type\":\"reasoning\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_atTkZSSGdblrFQLpEzqqLxp0|","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"C:\\Users\\Raitis\\Desktop\\My WEB projects\\SEOIndicator-com\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\package.json"},"partialJson":"{\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Raitis\\\\Desktop\\\\My WEB projects\\\\SEOIndicator-com\\\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\\\package.json\"}"}],"api":"openai-responses","provider":"github-copilot","model":"gpt-5.2-codex","usage":{"input":1184,"output":62,"cacheRead":8064,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":9310,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770895552470}}
{"type":"message","id":"a796202d","parentId":"25a4b8cd","timestamp":"2026-02-12T11:25:54.688Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_atTkZSSGdblrFQLpEzqqLxp0|","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\r\n  \"name\": \"seoindicator-tests\",\r\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Automated tests for SEOIndicator.com using Playwright\",\r\n  \"main\": \"index.js\",\r\n  \"scripts\": {\r\n    \"test\": \"playwright test\",\r\n    \"test:headed\": \"playwright test --headed\",\r\n    \"test:ui\": \"playwright test --ui\",\r\n    \"test:debug\": \"playwright test --debug\",\r\n    \"test:report\": \"playwright test --reporter=html\",\r\n    \"test:show-report\": \"playwright show-report\",\r\n    \"test:production\": \"cross-env BASE_URL=https://seoindicator.com playwright test\",\r\n    \"test:production:headed\": \"cross-env BASE_URL=https://seoindicator.com playwright test --headed\",\r\n    \"test:production:ui\": \"cross-env BASE_URL=https://seoindicator.com playwright test --ui\",\r\n    \"test:production:debug\": \"cross-env BASE_URL=https://seoindicator.com playwright test --debug\",\r\n    \"test:production:report\": \"cross-env BASE_URL=https://seoindicator.com playwright test --reporter=html\",\r\n    \"install:browsers\": \"playwright install --with-deps\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"keywords\": [\r\n    \"playwright\",\r\n    \"testing\",\r\n    \"seo\",\r\n    \"automation\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"author\": \"\",\r\n  \"license\": \"MIT\",\r\n  \"devDependencies\": {\r\n    \"@playwright/test\": \"^1.40.0\",\r\n    \"cross-env\": \"^10.0.0\"\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770895554686}}
{"type":"message","id":"469ca254","parentId":"a796202d","timestamp":"2026-02-12T11:25:57.454Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Checking deployment and test instructions**\n\nI'm verifying deployment steps and deciding to run tests in production mode to validate local header changes; I'll review docs/HOSTINGER-DEPLOYMENT-SETUP.md for deployment details.","thinkingSignature":"{\"encrypted_content\":\"\",\"id\":\"\",\"summary\":[{\"text\":\"**Checking deployment and test instructions**\\n\\nI'm verifying deployment steps and deciding to run tests in production mode to validate local header changes; I'll review docs/HOSTINGER-DEPLOYMENT-SETUP.md for deployment details.\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"}],\"type\":\"reasoning\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_QTh5eB1cZhgbx4YUtbSgru6x|","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"C:\\Users\\Raitis\\Desktop\\My WEB projects\\SEOIndicator-com\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\docs\\HOSTINGER-DEPLOYMENT-SETUP.md"},"partialJson":"{\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Raitis\\\\Desktop\\\\My WEB projects\\\\SEOIndicator-com\\\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\\\docs\\\\HOSTINGER-DEPLOYMENT-SETUP.md\"}"}],"api":"openai-responses","provider":"github-copilot","model":"gpt-5.2-codex","usage":{"input":558,"output":114,"cacheRead":9088,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":9760,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770895554689}}
{"type":"message","id":"fa1a671b","parentId":"469ca254","timestamp":"2026-02-12T11:25:57.499Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_QTh5eB1cZhgbx4YUtbSgru6x|","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Hostinger Automated Deployment Setup\r\n\r\nThis guide explains how to set up automated deployment from GitHub Actions to your Hostinger shared hosting account.\r\n\r\n## 🎯 **What This Provides**\r\n\r\n- ✅ **Automatic deployment** on every push to main branch\r\n- ✅ **Production testing** after deployment\r\n- ✅ **Failed test logs** for debugging\r\n- ✅ **Secure FTP deployment** to Hostinger\r\n- ✅ **File filtering** (excludes development files)\r\n\r\n## 🔧 **Setup Instructions**\r\n\r\n### 1. Get Hostinger FTP Credentials\r\n\r\n1. **Login to Hostinger Control Panel**\r\n2. **Go to File Manager** or **FTP Accounts**\r\n3. **Note down these details:**\r\n   - FTP Host (usually: `ftp.yourdomain.com` or IP address)\r\n   - FTP Username (usually: `yourdomain.com` or custom)\r\n   - FTP Password\r\n\r\n### 2. Add GitHub Secrets\r\n\r\n1. **Go to your GitHub repository**\r\n2. **Click Settings** → **Secrets and variables** → **Actions**\r\n3. **Add these repository secrets:**\r\n\r\n```\r\nHOSTINGER_FTP_HOST = ftp.yourdomain.com\r\nHOSTINGER_FTP_USERNAME = yourdomain.com\r\nHOSTINGER_FTP_PASSWORD = your_ftp_password\r\n```\r\n\r\n### 3. File Structure on Hostinger\r\n\r\nYour files will be deployed to `/public_html/` directory:\r\n\r\n```\r\npublic_html/\r\n├── index.php\r\n├── style.css\r\n├── api/\r\n├── seo-guides/\r\n├── config.php\r\n├── db_config.php\r\n└── ... (other PHP files)\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Excluded files** (won't be deployed):\r\n- `.git/` and `.github/`\r\n- `node_modules/`\r\n- `tests/` and `test-logs/`\r\n- `package.json` and `playwright.config.js`\r\n- Development files\r\n\r\n## 🚀 **Workflow Overview**\r\n\r\n### **Deploy and Test Workflow** (`.github/workflows/deploy-and-test.yml`)\r\n\r\n1. **Deploy Phase:**\r\n   - Checkout code\r\n   - Install dependencies\r\n   - Deploy to Hostinger via FTP\r\n   - Wait for deployment propagation\r\n\r\n2. **Test Phase:**\r\n   - Install Playwright browsers\r\n   - Run tests against production site\r\n   - Generate failure logs if tests fail\r\n   - Commit logs to repository\r\n\r\n### **Separate Test Workflow** (`.github/workflows/playwright.yml`)\r\n\r\n- Runs tests against production site\r\n- No deployment (for testing only)\r\n- Useful for testing without deploying\r\n\r\n## 📋 **Deployment Process**\r\n\r\n### **Automatic Deployment:**\r\n```bash\r\ngit add .\r\ngit commit -m \"Update website\"\r\ngit push origin main\r\n```\r\n\r\n**What happens:**\r\n1. ✅ **Code deploys** to Hostinger\r\n2. ✅ **Tests run** against production\r\n3. ✅ **Success/ failure** reported in GitHub Actions\r\n4. ✅ **Logs created** if tests fail\r\n\r\n### **Manual Deployment:**\r\n- Go to **Actions** tab in GitHub\r\n- Click **Deploy and Test Production**\r\n- Click **Run workflow**\r\n\r\n## 🔒 **Security Features**\r\n\r\n- ✅ **FTP credentials** stored as encrypted secrets\r\n- ✅ **No sensitive files** deployed (config.php, .env)\r\n- ✅ **Development files** excluded\r\n- ✅ **Secure SFTP** connection\r\n\r\n## 🐛 **Troubleshooting**\r\n\r\n### **Deployment Fails:**\r\n1. **Check FTP credentials** in GitHub secrets\r\n2. **Verify FTP host** is correct\r\n3. **Check Hostinger** file permissions\r\n4. **Review deployment logs** in GitHub Actions\r\n\r\n### **Tests Fail After Deployment:**\r\n1. **Check production site** manually: https://seoindicator.com\r\n2. **Review test logs** in `test-logs/` directory\r\n3. **Verify file upload** was successful\r\n4. **Check for PHP errors** in Hostinger logs\r\n\r\n### **Site Not Accessible:**\r\n1. **Check file permissions** on Hostinger\r\n2. **Verify index.php** was uploaded\r\n3. **Check .htaccess** file (if any)\r\n4. **Review Hostinger** error logs\r\n\r\n## 📊 **Monitoring**\r\n\r\n### **Success Indicators:**\r\n- ✅ **Green checkmark** in GitHub Actions\r\n- ✅ **Site accessible** at https://seoindicator.com\r\n- ✅ **Tests passing** in production\r\n\r\n### **Failure Indicators:**\r\n- ❌ **Red X** in GitHub Actions\r\n- ❌ **Failed test logs** in repository\r\n- ❌ **Site not accessible** or errors\r\n\r\n## 🎉 **Benefits**\r\n\r\n- ✅ **Zero-downtime deployment** (files upload directly)\r\n- ✅ **Automatic testing** after deployment\r\n- ✅ **Version control** integration\r\n- ✅ **Rollback capability** (git revert)\r\n- ✅ **Team collaboration** (multiple developers)\r\n- ✅ **Production monitoring** (automated tests)\r\n\r\n## 🔄 **Workflow Customization**\r\n\r\n### **Change Deployment Branch:**\r\nEdit `.github/workflows/deploy-and-test.yml`:\r\n```yaml\r\non:\r\n  push:\r\n    branches: [ main, develop ]  # Add your branches\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Exclude More Files:**\r\nAdd to the `exclude` section:\r\n```yaml\r\nexclude: |\r\n  **/.git*\r\n  **/your-custom-file.txt\r\n  **/temp/**\r\n```\r\n\r\n### **Add Build Step:**\r\nIf you need to build assets:\r\n```yaml\r\n- name: Build assets\r\n  run: |\r\n    npm run build\r\n    # Add your build commands\r\n```\r\n\r\n## 📞 **Support**\r\n\r\nIf you encounter issues:\r\n1. **Check GitHub Actions logs** for detailed error messages\r\n2. **Verify Hostinger** FTP settings\r\n3. **Test FTP connection** manually\r\n4. **Review this guide** for common solutions\r\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770895557497}}
{"type":"message","id":"812410f2","parentId":"fa1a671b","timestamp":"2026-02-12T11:26:01.441Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Confirming deployment is manual via GitHub Actions**\n\nAuto deployment on push is disabled per workflow edits, so deployment requires a manual trigger of the Actions workflow; next, I'll verify this and check if the environment supports git commands to run commits and pushes.","thinkingSignature":"{\"encrypted_content\":\"\",\"id\":\"\",\"summary\":[{\"text\":\"**Confirming deployment is manual via GitHub Actions**\\n\\nAuto deployment on push is disabled per workflow edits, so deployment requires a manual trigger of the Actions workflow; next, I'll verify this and check if the environment supports git commands to run commits and pushes.\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"}],\"type\":\"reasoning\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_wxBLAWaHkLThNUzwrLkja2Us|","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"git status -sb","workdir":"C:\\Users\\Raitis\\Desktop\\My WEB projects\\SEOIndicator-com\\Files-SEOIndicator-com"},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"git status -sb\",\"workdir\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Raitis\\\\Desktop\\\\My WEB projects\\\\SEOIndicator-com\\\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\"}"}],"api":"openai-responses","provider":"github-copilot","model":"gpt-5.2-codex","usage":{"input":1379,"output":172,"cacheRead":9600,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":11151,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770895557499}}
