{"type":"message","id":"5dc68a41","parentId":"c20244ef","timestamp":"2026-02-12T11:26:09.475Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Clarifying deployment and test scope**\n\nModified tests may be unrelated and should not be committed; only index.php with XXX removal will be staged and pushed after pulling remote changes. Deployment might use ftp or a manual GitHub Action. I'll run automated production tests post-deployment to validate.\n\n**Assessing deployment trigger options**\n\nAuto deployment is disabled, but a manual GitHub workflow exists and might be triggerable via the GitHub CLI. I'll review the deploy-and-test workflow to confirm how deployment and testing can be initiated.","thinkingSignature":"{\"encrypted_content\":\"\",\"id\":\"\",\"summary\":[{\"text\":\"**Clarifying deployment and test scope**\\n\\nModified tests may be unrelated and should not be committed; only index.php with XXX removal will be staged and pushed after pulling remote changes. Deployment might use ftp or a manual GitHub Action. I'll run automated production tests post-deployment to validate.\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"},{\"text\":\"**Assessing deployment trigger options**\\n\\nAuto deployment is disabled, but a manual GitHub workflow exists and might be triggerable via the GitHub CLI. I'll review the deploy-and-test workflow to confirm how deployment and testing can be initiated.\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"}],\"type\":\"reasoning\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_mp50v4RR6qJ29fYBspWPFGeh|","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"C:\\Users\\Raitis\\Desktop\\My WEB projects\\SEOIndicator-com\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\.github\\workflows\\deploy-and-test.yml"},"partialJson":"{\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Raitis\\\\Desktop\\\\My WEB projects\\\\SEOIndicator-com\\\\Files-SEOIndicator-com\\\\.github\\\\workflows\\\\deploy-and-test.yml\"}"}],"api":"openai-responses","provider":"github-copilot","model":"gpt-5.2-codex","usage":{"input":179,"output":410,"cacheRead":11008,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":11597,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770895561784}}
{"type":"message","id":"dff82916","parentId":"5dc68a41","timestamp":"2026-02-12T11:26:09.501Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_mp50v4RR6qJ29fYBspWPFGeh|","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"name: Deploy and Test Production\r\n\r\non:\r\n  workflow_dispatch:\r\n\r\njobs:\r\n  deploy:\r\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\r\n    permissions:\r\n      contents: write\r\n    outputs:\r\n      deployed: ${{ steps.deploy.outcome == 'success' }}\r\n    \r\n    steps:\r\n    - name: Checkout code\r\n      uses: actions/checkout@v4\r\n    \r\n    - name: Setup Node.js\r\n      uses: actions/setup-node@v4\r\n      with:\r\n        node-version: lts/*\r\n        cache: 'npm'\r\n    \r\n    - name: Disable man-db triggers for faster apt operations\r\n      run: |\r\n        echo \"set man-db/auto-update false\" | sudo debconf-communicate\r\n        sudo dpkg-reconfigure man-db\r\n    \r\n    - name: Install dependencies\r\n      run: npm ci --prefer-offline --no-audit --no-fund\r\n    \r\n    - name: Deploy to Hostinger\r\n      id: deploy\r\n      uses: SamKirkland/FTP-Deploy-Action@v4.3.4\r\n      with:\r\n        server: ${{ secrets.HOSTINGER_FTP_HOST }}\r\n        username: ${{ secrets.HOSTINGER_FTP_USERNAME }}\r\n        password: ${{ secrets.HOSTINGER_FTP_PASSWORD }}\r\n        server-dir: /public_html/\r\n        exclude: |\r\n          **/.git*\r\n          **/.git*/**\r\n          **/node_modules/**\r\n          **/.github/**\r\n          **/tests/**\r\n          **/prod-test-results/**\r\n          **/local-test-results/**\r\n          **/ci-test-results/**\r\n          **/playwright-report/**\r\n          **/.env\r\n          **/config.php\r\n          **/db_config.php\r\n          **/package.json\r\n          **/package-lock.json\r\n          **/playwright.config.js\r\n          **/CI-SETUP.md\r\n          **/README.md\r\n          **/to_do.txt\r\n          **/to_fix.txt\r\n          **/project_overview.txt\r\n    \r\n    - name: Wait for deployment\r\n      run: sleep 15  # Reduced wait time for faster execution\r\n\r\n  test-production:\r\n    needs: deploy\r\n    if: needs.deploy.outputs.deployed == 'true'\r\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\r\n    timeout-minutes: 15\r\n    permissions:\r\n      contents: write\r\n    \r\n    steps:\r\n    - name: Checkout code\r\n      uses: actions/checkout@v4\r\n    \r\n    - name: Setup Node.js\r\n      uses: actions/setup-node@v4\r\n      with:\r\n        node-version: lts/*\r\n        cache: 'npm'\r\n    \r\n    - name: Disable man-db triggers for faster apt operations\r\n      run: |\r\n        echo \"set man-db/auto-update false\" | sudo debconf-communicate\r\n        sudo dpkg-reconfigure man-db\r\n    \r\n    - name: Install dependencies\r\n      run: npm ci --prefer-offline --no-audit --no-fund\r\n    \r\n    - name: Cache Playwright browsers\r\n      uses: actions/cache@v4\r\n      id: playwright-cache\r\n      with:\r\n        path: |\r\n          ~/.cache/ms-playwright\r\n        key: playwright-chrome-${{ hashFiles('package-lock.json') }}\r\n        restore-keys: |\r\n          playwright-chrome-\r\n          playwright-browsers-\r\n    \r\n    - name: Install Playwright Browsers\r\n      if: steps.playwright-cache.outputs.cache-hit != 'true'\r\n      run: npx playwright install --with-deps chrome\r\n    \r\n    - name: Run Production Tests\r\n      run: |\r\n        npx playwright test --max-failures=1 --workers=2 --reporter=github 2>&1 | tee test-output.log\r\n        exit ${PIPESTATUS[0]}\r\n    \r\n    - name: Generate Failed Tests Log\r\n      if: failure()\r\n      run: |\r\n        echo \"# Production Test Failure Report - $(date)\" > failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"## Deployment & Test Summary\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"- **Date**: $(date)\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"- **Commit**: ${{ github.sha }}\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"- **Branch**: ${{ github.ref_name }}\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"- **Deployed to**: https://seoindicator.com\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"- **Test Environment**: Production\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"## Test Output\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        \r\n        if [ -f \"test-output.log\" ]; then\r\n          echo \"### Console Output\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n          echo '```' >> failed-tests.md\r\n          tail -50 test-output.log >> failed-tests.md\r\n          echo '```' >> failed-tests.md\r\n          echo \"\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        fi\r\n        \r\n        echo \"### Environment Information\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"- **OS**: $(uname -a)\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"- **Node Version**: $(node --version)\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"- **Playwright Version**: $(npx playwright --version)\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"- **Browser**: Chrome (stable channel)\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"- **Target URL**: https://seoindicator.com\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        \r\n        echo \"## Next Steps\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"1. Check the production site: https://seoindicator.com\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"2. Review test failures and fix issues\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"3. Re-run tests after fixes\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n        echo \"4. Check deployment logs if site is not accessible\" >> failed-tests.md\r\n    \r\n    - name: Upload Failed Tests Log\r\n      if: failure()\r\n      uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4\r\n      with:\r\n        name: production-test-failure\r\n        path: failed-tests.md\r\n        retention-days: 30\r\n    \r\n    - name: Commit Failed Test Log to Repository\r\n      if: failure()\r\n      run: |\r\n        if [ -f \"failed-tests.md\" ]; then\r\n          TIMESTAMP=$(date +\"%Y%m%d_%H%M%S\")\r\n          COMMIT_SHORT=$(echo \"${{ github.sha }}\" | cut -c1-7)\r\n          FILENAME=\"prod-test-results/production_failed_tests_${TIMESTAMP}_${COMMIT_SHORT}.md\"\r\n          \r\n          mkdir -p prod-test-results\r\n          mv failed-tests.md \"$FILENAME\"\r\n          \r\n          {\r\n            echo \"# Production Test Failure Report\"\r\n            echo \"\"\r\n            echo \"**Workflow Run**: [${{ github.server_url }}/${{ github.repository }}/actions/runs/${{ github.run_id }}](${{ github.server_url }}/${{ github.repository }}/actions/runs/${{ github.run_id }})\"\r\n            echo \"**Commit**: [${{ github.sha }}](${{ github.server_url }}/${{ github.repository }}/commit/${{ github.sha }})\"\r\n            echo \"**Branch**: ${{ github.ref_name }}\"\r\n            echo \"**Deployed to**: https://seoindicator.com\"\r\n            echo \"**Date**: $(date)\"\r\n            echo \"\"\r\n            echo \"---\"\r\n            echo \"\"\r\n            cat \"$FILENAME\"\r\n          } > \"$FILENAME.tmp\" && mv \"$FILENAME.tmp\" \"$FILENAME\"\r\n          \r\n          git config --local user.email \"action@github.com\"\r\n          git config --local user.name \"GitHub Action\"\r\n          \r\n          git add \"$FILENAME\"\r\n          git commit -m \"Add production test failure log from workflow run ${{ github.run_id }}\" || echo \"No changes to commit\"\r\n          \r\n          git push origin HEAD:${{ github.ref_name }} || echo \"Failed to push changes\"\r\n        fi\r\n    \r\n    - name: Upload Playwright Report\r\n      if: always()\r\n      uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4\r\n      with:\r\n        name: production-playwright-report\r\n        path: playwright-report/\r\n        retention-days: 30\r\n        if-no-files-found: ignore\r\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770895569498}}
{"type":"message","id":"2c7ae345","parentId":"dff82916","timestamp":"2026-02-12T11:26:23.025Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Assessing safe git workflow for manual deploy**\n\nI'm weighing how to update the repo amidst local uncommitted changes and being behind remote; stashing tests locally to pull updates before committing index.php seems safest to avoid conflicts without losing modifications. Next, I'll confirm if `gh workflow run` can trigger deployment after pushing.\n\n**Planning git rebase with autostash for push**\n\nI'll use `git pull --rebase --autostash` to safely update the repo while preserving all local changes, then stage and commit only the index.php change before pushing. Afterward, I'll trigger the deployment workflow via the gh CLI if installed.","thinkingSignature":"{\"encrypted_content\":\"\",\"id\":\"\",\"summary\":[{\"text\":\"**Assessing safe git workflow for manual deploy**\\n\\nI'm weighing how to update the repo amidst local uncommitted changes and being behind remote; stashing tests locally to pull updates before committing index.php seems safest to avoid conflicts without losing modifications. Next, I'll confirm if `gh workflow run` can trigger deployment after pushing.\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"},{\"text\":\"**Planning git rebase with autostash for push**\\n\\nI'll use `git pull --rebase --autostash` to safely update the repo while preserving all local changes, then stage and commit only the index.php change before pushing. Afterward, I'll trigger the deployment workflow via the gh CLI if installed.\",\"type\":\"summary_text\"}],\"type\":\"reasoning\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_qyIqeOihInbO0mCmYGI8eH4U|","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"gh --version","workdir":"C:\\Users\\Raitis\\Desktop\\My WEB projects\\SEOIndicator-com\\Files-SEOIndicator-com"},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"gh --version\",\"workdir\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Raitis\\\\Desktop\\\\My WEB projects\\\\SEOIndicator-com\\\\Fi